  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community-Based Waste Management (CBWM) Project operated by COERR will sustain and strengthen the vital waste management services in Mae La refugee camp and six surrounding Thai host villages, directly safeguarding public health, environmental protection, and promoting community empowerment, serving 45,088 people, consisting of all 38,670 refugees living in Mae La camp and 6,418 host community members, and is implemented through a participant-centered, community-led model that builds on the engagement and skills of refugee volunteers working in close coordination with Thai authorities</narrative>
  </description>
